ransducer block" description="Name" type="1" show="0"/><FIELD pos="-23.17890625,-8.5" value="BLK4" description="Ref" type="0" show="1"/><FIELD pos="-39.4,-8" value="1" description="Gain" type="1" show="0"/><FIELD pos="-39.4,-8" value="100k" description="Bandwidth" type="1" show="0"/><FIELD pos="-39.4,-8" value="TinyCAD configurable educational equivalent" description="Simulation model" type="1" show="0"/></SYMBOL><WIRE a="94,87" b="86,87"/><LABEL pos="86,87" font="3" color="432D14" direction="3" style="0">RECEIVED</LABEL><WIRE a="134,87" b="145,87"/><LABEL pos="134.69203124999999,87" font="3" color="432D14" direction="3" style="0">OUTPUT</LABEL><NOTE_TEXT a="7,4" b="233,16.6" font="4" color="432D14" style="3" fill="0" direction="3" border_style="0">A39 · Electronic communication-chain connections</NOTE_TEXT><NOTE_TEXT a="147,21" b="233,148" font="1" color="432D14" style="4" fill="2" direction="3" border_style="0">## Follow the system interfaces

**Post-16 · ages 16–19**

A system diagram shows where signals enter, how they are conditioned and where the results are used. Labelled connections describe interfaces; physical and software behaviour need separate evidence.

### Your investigation

Follow each signal from source to destination. Mark the reference, expected voltage range, loading and useful test points. Explain how you would test each stage.

### This activity

Draw and annotate source, processing, transmitter, channel and receiver blocks. Identify which interfaces carry electrical signals. This is a block-diagram teaching exercise, not an end-to-end communication simulation.

### Getting started

This is a connection-planning drawing. Follow each labelled net, identify the real terminals and add your bench measurements. No simulation is attached.

The buffer represents a processing stage; choose suitable analogue conditioning for a real sensor. Follow SENSOR → CONDITIONED → TX → RX → RECEIVED. The final physical output is a system label.

**Explain:** Use an equation, a truth table or a state sequence to justify your prediction. Include units and discuss the model assumptions.

Check the physical layout with your teacher before construction.</NOTE_TEXT></TinyCAD><DSNSETTINGS><SHOW_RULERS>1</SHOW_RULERS></DSNSETTINGS><NETLIST_TYPES><TYPE name="default"/></NETLIST_TYPES></TinyCADSheets>